course: dictionary
lesson: 6836
title: Outdoors: one word, three jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Outdoors means outside, not inside a building. In «Fire and water give us lots of fun outdoors», the word tells you where the fun happens, so it is an adverb.
explain: Put the word next to a noun and it changes its job. In «outdoor activities», outdoor describes the activities, so it is an adjective. Add the in front and it becomes a noun: «the outdoors» means the natural world away from buildings, such as fields, woods, mountains and beaches.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «Lightning kills people every year, most of them outdoors near water, on high ground or under tall trees.» Water, high ground and tall trees are all places out in nature, so outdoors must mean out in the open air, away from buildings.
explain: «Weather changes what is safe outdoors.» Being outdoors is fun, but it needs care. Check the weather, tell an adult where you are going, and stay safe.
fact: Outdoors means outside, not in a building.
fact: «Camping means living outdoors for a while, so you choose a safe place for the tent.»
fact: The outdoors is the natural world away from buildings: fields, woods, mountains and beaches.
fact: Outdoor is an adjective, as in «outdoor activities».
fact: «Research suggests time outdoors in daylight lowers the risk of children becoming short-sighted.»
exercise: In «Fire and water give us lots of fun outdoors», what kind of word is outdoors? | A describing word before a noun | A verb, showing an action | A noun, naming a thing | *An adverb, telling where the fun happens
exercise: Which word in «outdoor activities» is the describing word? | neither | activities | *outdoor | both
exercise: What does «the outdoors» mean? | *The natural world away from buildings, such as fields and woods | A type of weather | The inside of a school hall | A shop that sells clothes
test: In «Lightning kills people every year, most of them outdoors near water, on high ground or under tall trees», what does outdoors mean? | In a classroom | Inside a house | Under a bed | *Out in the open air, away from buildings
test: Which step keeps you safe when you are outdoors? | Ignore the weather | Forget your hat and sunscreen | *Tell an adult where you are going | Walk off alone without telling anyone
exam: Which sentence uses outdoors as a noun? | *Hikers love the outdoors and its wide fields. | Children play outdoors at break. | Their outdoor jacket is warm. | They walked outdoors.
